# Task: adversarial review of `docs/design/dao.lease.md`

Role: Lead Systems Architecture Reviewer

## What this is

`docs/design/dao.lease.md` now exists. It is a reconciliation of five
independent drafts — yours among them — written by the orchestrator. Your own
proposal was one input; the document is not your draft and you owe it no
loyalty.

Review it as a document that must stand on its own.

## Scope

Read:

- docs/design/dao.lease.md          — under review
- docs/design/datom.world.md        — the governing authority
- docs/design/jit-design.md         — the precedent it claims to follow
- docs/design/dao.stream.md         — the contract it claims not to touch
- docs/design/dao.stream.ws.md      — where carriage is said to live

**No source code.** No ADRs, no `dao.space` documents, no `collab/` logs.

## What to test

1. **Does it hold together?** Section against section. In particular: the
   negotiation vocabulary against "silence is absence"; the observed-window
   discipline against the clock rules; "lapse is a conclusion, reclaim is an
   act" against the obligation section.
2. **Is the precedent claim honest?** It asserts it is the second instance of
   `jit-design.md`'s pattern and names three divergences. Check the mapping
   against that document rather than against the claim. If a fourth divergence
   exists, or one of the three is spurious, say so.
3. **Does it in fact touch nothing?** It claims to add no operation, no
   component, and no key to any DaoStream result map, and that
   `dao.stream.md` is unchanged by its existence. Verify against those
   documents, both directions: something it changes without saying, and
   something it needs that no document grants.
4. **Is the reconciliation sound where the drafts disagreed?** One split was
   real: whether the negotiation lifecycle belongs in the vocabulary at all.
   The document keeps `:proposed`/`:accepted`/`:rejected` and adds "a proposal
   creates no state — an unanswered proposal is not pending and is not queued."
   Judge that resolution. If you argued the other side, say whether the added
   rule answers your objection or papers over it.
5. **What would an implementer have to invent?** Someone building a grantor
   and a holder from this document alone.
6. **What is missing that no draft raised?** The five drafts converged; that is
   a reason for suspicion, not confidence.

## Output

Findings ranked most severe first: severity | section or line | the claim | the
exact correction. Then one short section: **the thing in this document most
likely to be wrong that I cannot prove is wrong.**

State plainly if you find nothing at a given severity. Read-only; make no
edits.

